diff --git a/scripts/svae_train/FEATURE_PROVENANCE.md b/scripts/svae_train/FEATURE_PROVENANCE.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..eff74a0
--- /dev/null
+++ b/scripts/svae_train/FEATURE_PROVENANCE.md
@@ -0,0 +1,22 @@
+# Optional sample provenance
+
+Pass `svae_collect.write_sample_provenance=true` to the normal feature collector.
+Default collection output and model/training behavior are unchanged. The enabled
+collector adds `provenance_version: 1` and one `sample_metadata` record per feature
+row to each existing shard; feature-only readers can continue ignoring extra keys.
+
+Each record contains the actual shuffled dataset index, the collection split
+(`train`, as in the existing collector), available task/episode/window fields,
+and SHA256 of the preprocessed encoder input with its dtype and shape. Hashing
+happens after dataset augmentation and encoder preprocessing. BF16 is hashed as
+raw bytes, not cast to a different numeric format. This adds CPU transfer and
+hashing overhead only when enabled.
+
+Use episode identities to audit externally defined train/evaluation manifests;
+this option does not itself split data or prove that caches are disjoint. It
+also does not save labels, augmentation parameters, all sampled raw-frame indices,
+or an encoder checkpoint hash. The existing resolved config remains available
+beside the shards. Missing dataset-specific metadata stays absent, not invented.
+A matching input digest establishes byte identity under the recorded dtype/shape,
+not semantic scene equivalence. Paths are recorded exactly as supplied by the
+dataset and may be machine specific.
